menu "c6 base (Wi-Fi, OTA, logs, claim)"

config C6_WIFI_SSID
    string "Wi-Fi SSID"
    default ""
    help
        Used once, when nothing is stored (0.5.0); empty in a public build.
        Leave empty in a public build; set it in your own sdkconfig.

config C6_WIFI_PASS
    string "Wi-Fi password"
    default ""
    help
        Used once, when nothing is stored (0.5.0); empty in a public build.
        Leave empty in a public build; set it in your own sdkconfig.

config C6_OTA_TOKEN
    string "Developer credential (X-OTA-Token)"
    default ""
    help
        The developer credential, also accepted by the claim-protected endpoints while set;
        empty in a public build. 16 to 79 characters, or every X-OTA-Token value is refused
        (more than 79 stops the build).
        Leave empty in a public build; set it in your own sdkconfig.

config C6_LED_GPIO
    int "Blue LED GPIO (held off)"
    default 7
    help
        The M5Stack NanoC6's blue LED. It is configured as an output and held off; every LED
        pattern is on the colour LED (C6_RGB_GPIO).

config C6_RGB_GPIO
    int "Colour LED (WS2812) data GPIO"
    default 20
    help
        The data line of the M5Stack NanoC6's colour LED, a WS2812 driven through the RMT.
        It shows the button's hold cues, the setup hotspot, an unclaimed board and /identify.

config C6_RGB_PWR_GPIO
    int "Colour LED power GPIO"
    default 19
    help
        The GPIO that switches the colour LED's power on the M5Stack NanoC6. Driven high at
        start.

config C6_RGB_LEVEL
    int "Colour LED brightness (0-255)"
    range 0 255
    default 40
    help
        Every colour the colour LED shows, the one /identify is given included, is scaled by
        this over 255. 0 keeps the LED dark.

config C6_BUTTON_GPIO
    int "Button GPIO (active low)"
    default 9
    help
        The M5Stack NanoC6's button. A press opens the claim window for 10 minutes, a 3-9 s hold
        opens the setup hotspot for 10 minutes, a 10 s hold clears the claim.

config C6_AP_SSID_PREFIX
    string "Setup hotspot SSID prefix"
    default "Zigbee-Anthema-"
    help
        The hotspot's SSID is this followed by the board's six-hex serial.

config C6_WIFI_FAIL_S
    int "Seconds without an IP before the hotspot opens"
    default 60
    help
        Seconds without an IP before the hotspot opens, counted from boot and from every new
        Wi-Fi setting.

config C6_VERIFY_TIMEOUT_S
    int "Seconds a new OTA image has to bring up Wi-Fi and HTTP before it is rolled back"
    default 120

config C6_WIFI_START_DELAY_MS
    int "Delay before Wi-Fi starts (diagnostic; 0 = at once)"
    default 0
    help
        Keep it well under C6_VERIFY_TIMEOUT_S, or a new image rolls back before Wi-Fi is up.

config C6_VERIFY_STABLE_S
    int "Seconds a new OTA image must then run without a reset before it is marked valid"
    default 60

config C6_VERIFY_ZIGBEE_S
    int "Seconds from boot a new OTA image has to get Zigbee back before it is rolled back"
    default 600
    help
        Seconds from boot a new image has to get Zigbee back (joined, or factory new) before it is
        rolled back, when the image asks for the check (c6_app_verify_zigbee). The default is
        10 minutes; a rejoin after an update takes 20 s to 3 min, once 24 min.

config C6_VERIFY_BREAK_TEST
    bool "Rollback test: never count Zigbee as back"
    default n
    help
        Rollback test only: c6_base_zigbee_ready() sets nothing, so a build with this on rolls back
        after C6_VERIFY_ZIGBEE_S with Wi-Fi, HTTP and Zigbee all up. Never in a release build;
        sdkconfig.defaults keeps it off.

endmenu
